.TH PCLOUDC 1 "2026-04-15" "pcloud-rs Rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pcloudc \- pCloud command-line client for the Rust rewrite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcloudc
[\fIGLOBAL-OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B pcloudc
[\fIGLOBAL-OPTIONS\fR]
.B login
[\fILOGIN-OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pcloudc
is the interactive and scripting client for the Rust-based pCloud daemon.
It talks to
.BR pcloudd (1)
over a local owner-only Unix socket, exposes account/session management,
sync-root control, crypto control, public-link operations, sharing helpers,
mount control, notifications, and audit verification.

The command surface retains many legacy
.B pcloud-rs
aliases for compatibility, but new scripts should prefer the canonical
.B pcloudc
forms documented here.
