.SH SECURITY NOTES
Prefer
.B login
over passing credentials on the command line. Interactive login keeps
passwords out of shell history and process listings where possible.

The CLI uses a local owner-checked Unix socket; secret-bearing IPC values still
cross the serialization boundary transiently, so avoid exposing the socket to
other users or relaxing runtime-directory permissions.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pcloud/
Default development root used by current secure-default bootstrap.
